{
  "_about": "laneVIS_ground v1 (ZoneGroundMat.cs, CODE once then HOT). Per-zone ground MATERIAL: under each zoneRoot the renderers whose material name contains matchMaterial (and not excludeMaterial) get ONE shared clone with ABSOLUTE _BaseColor = tint (the original assets are _BaseColor 1,1,1, so this also replaces the wetness.json 0.6 darkening on the ground), smoothness remap min/max, normal scale, detail albedo/normal/smoothness scale (the _DETAIL_MAP keyword is already on both ground materials: macro blotches, no shader variant), tiling multipliers (relative to the existing _BaseColorMap_ST / _DetailMap_ST) and an optional texture swap from StreamingAssets/groundmat. mix 0..1 blends tint and tiling from today (log-space) so Dom can dial a look. -1 = leave. enabled=false ships dark.",
  "enabled": true,
  "log": true,
  "rescanSeconds": 3.0,
  "settledRescanSeconds": 20.0,
  "maxPerPoll": 60,
  "texDir": "groundmat",
  "cloneSuffix": " (zgm)",
